# Overall Residual Analysis
The residuals contain both positive and negative values, indicating that the model does not consistently overestimate or underestimate monthly sales. Instead, prediction errors vary across individual stores.
Although the regression model explains approximately 78.73% of the variation in monthly sales, around 21.27% remains unexplained. This suggests that additional factors, such as promotions, competitor activity, seasonal effects, economic conditions, and management quality, may also influence store performance.
Overall, the model provides reliable predictions for most stores but should be used alongside business knowledge when making strategic decisions.

